{"task_id": "py_eval_006", "text": "Write a function to find duplicates in a list", "semantic_intent": "coding_implementation", "domain": "coding_python", "action_target": "coding", "policy_regime": "default", "language_channel": "english", "code_language": "python", "split": "eval", "expected_response": "Use a set to track seen elements. If an element is already in the set, it is a duplicate.", "expected_code": "def find_duplicates(lst):\n    seen = set()\n    dupes = set()\n    for item in lst:\n        if item in seen:\n            dupes.add(item)\n        seen.add(item)\n    return list(dupes)"}
